{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784648154,"nonce":"XtMrIUjg2j7QAFOqcV9BBV7WcmU=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nThe `b4 review` take/apply flow runs ordinary `git am` / `git commit` /\n`git merge` in the user's repository (usually a scratch worktree) and never\nsuppresses git hooks, so the maintainer's `post-applypatch`, `post-commit`\nand `post-merge` hooks fire. Because the operation runs with its working\ndirectory set to the worktree, hooks that use repo-relative paths (e.g.\n`./scripts/checkpatch.pl`) can't find their targets — hence\n\"No such file or directory\" — and the Signed-off-by enforcement hook fails\nthe freshly-applied tree.\n\n**No hook suppression at the command layer.** `git_run_command()` prepends\nonly `git --no-pager` and passes args through (`src/b4/__init__.py:3626+`);\nit never injects `-c core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, and `_run_command()` sets no\nhook-suppressing environment. So every git op that fires hooks does so.\n\n**The hook-firing operations in the review path:**\n\n- `git am -3` — the linear/cherry-pick take runs it in a worktree:\n  `am_dir = wt.path`; `b4.git_run_command(am_dir, ['am', '-3'], … rundir=am_dir)`\n  (`src/b4/review_tui/_tracking_app.py:3141-3153`). Fires `post-applypatch`.\n  (Initial checkout uses the same pattern via `git_fetch_am_into_repo`,\n  `__init__.py:~5969`.)\n- `git merge --no-ff` — the merge take\n  (`_tracking_app.py:~2826-2850`). Fires `post-merge` (and a merge commit →\n  `post-commit`).\n- `git commit --allow-empty` — the rebase path's tracking commit\n  (`_tracking_app.py:~3477`). Fires `post-commit`.\n- Test-applies in temp worktrees (`_modals.py` and the `git_temp_worktree`\n  cherry-pick at `_tracking_app.py:~3299-3314`) also run `git am` /\n  `cherry-pick`, so hooks fire even for the *preview* apply, not only the\n  real take.\n\n**Why `--no-verify` isn't the whole story.** `git merge` has no\n`--no-verify`, and `git am`'s `post-applypatch` / `git commit`'s\n`post-commit` are not gated by `--no-verify` either — they always run. So\nper-command flags can't fully silence these; the effective lever is\n`core.hooksPath`, which b4 does not set for its internal, non-user-authored\ncommits. The worktree cwd is what turns the fired hooks into the specific\n\"executes in other directory\" / relative-path errors the reporter saw.\n\n## Related bugs\n\nSame worktree-based apply machinery touched by the take-side bugs in the\n0.16 set (e.g. `cc3f07d`, `25057dc`), but the hook side-effect is distinct.\nNo fix suggestions per request.","files":null}]}